    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the record is unusually clear and both advocates read the key numbers the same way.\n\nWhat happened: the driver tapped 'I'm Here' at 14:22:40 and the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02754) puts him 1.1 m from the pickup pin at that instant, stationary at 0.0 km/h. The arrival marker is genuine and POL-NS-05 does not fire — no false-arrival referral is recorded against the driver. But the free waiting period in force for this STANDARD-zone trip is 180 seconds (EV-TRIP-02754, platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180). His longest continuous in-geofence dwell was 57 seconds (14:22:40 to 14:23:37, 7 qualifying fixes), a shortfall of 123 seconds, and he cancelled at 14:23:41. POL-NS-01 limb (c) fails and limb (d) fails with it, because the cancellation did not fall at or after the required dwell. POL-NS-06 then applies directly and is strict about it: where the effective in-geofence dwell is shorter than the free waiting period, the cancellation fee is not chargeable and is refunded in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she responded.\n\nThe rider was in fact present and trying to coordinate: her device shows 19 stationary fixes never more than 7.4 m from the pin, inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius, and she sent 'coming out now' at 14:23:40, one second before the cancellation. The driver neither replied within 120 seconds nor made any in-app call (trip_record.in_app_calls is empty). POL-NS-04 points the same way; the refund already follows from POL-NS-06, so nothing turns on it.\n\nThe money: EV-FARE-02754 shows the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee charged (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00, total_charged 4.50). The whole SGD 4.50 is refunded. No driver compensation is payable — POL-NS-07 compensates only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and POL-NS-06 displaces it. No POL-NS-03 pin-ambiguity goodwill (2.25) applies, because the driver's stationary fixes were inside the arrival radius, not outside it.\n\nPoints raised that do not change this: the driver's counterparty statement asking us to check the rider's 'history of no-shows' is not a ground of decision. POL-GEN-01 makes prior_no_show_flags (6) context-only; the only citable counter, rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d, reads 1, below the POL-NS-09(d) threshold of 3, and both profiles' disputes_with_counterparty_90d read 0. The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 1 against completed_trips_30d 58, rate 0.017), so there is no escalation and no withholding of compensation on that ground. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02754-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0); it bears only on POL-NS-06(i)'s accumulation route, which is unavailable and in any event unnecessary — there was a single 57-second interval to measure.\n\nWeight and confidence: the artifacts carrying the deciding facts, EV-GPS-02754 and EV-TRIP-02754, are both at weight_multiplier 1.0, and nothing is impaired under POL-NS-08 (no clock skew, no trace gap, chat sequence intact, fare line reconciles to the platform-published SGD 4.50). The monetary effect of SGD 4.50 is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so this ruling executes automatically. Either party may appeal within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
